# Milestone: v0.10.2-reactive (W0)
# Covers: whenever (named_event) {body} fires on every event emission.
#         Reactive audit F1 / roadmap F5 / Pico v0.9.4 finding.
#
# Semantics: whenever (e?) re-fires on EVERY event emission — perpetual
#   subscriber.  Distinct from at (e?) which is a one-shot subscriber.
#   The body re-arms automatically; no explicit teardown/re-install needed.
#
# Note: W6 (sleep built-in) has not yet merged; however the body
#   coroutines drain before the final Realm.tick_count read because the
#   cooperative scheduler yields between each statement.  No sleep/yield
#   workaround needed.
#
# Activated: 2026-05-25 as part of v0.10.2-reactive W0.

Realm.tick_count = 0
var e = Event.new()
whenever (e?) { Realm.tick_count = Realm.tick_count + 1 }
e!
e!
e!
Realm.tick_count
[00000000] 0
[00000000] <event>
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 3
